{"route":"/docs/5.2/getting-started/rtl/","version":"5.2","renderedVersion":"5.2","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"RTL","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Learn how to enable support for right-to-left text in Bootstrap across our layout, components, and utilities."},"blocks":[{"id":"get-familiar","type":"heading","en":"Get familiar","level":2},{"id":"get-familiar--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"We recommend getting familiar with Bootstrap first by reading through our <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/introduction/\">Getting Started Introduction page</a>. Once you’ve run through it, continue reading here for how to enable RTL."},{"id":"get-familiar--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"You may also want to read up on <a href=\"https://rtlcss.com/\">the RTLCSS project</a>, as it powers our approach to RTL."},{"id":"get-familiar--note-1","type":"note","tone":"warning","body":[{"id":"experimental-feature","type":"heading","en":"Experimental feature","level":3},{"id":"experimental-feature--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"The RTL feature is still <strong>experimental</strong> and will probably evolve according to user feedback. Spotted something or have an improvement to suggest? <a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/issues/new/choose\">Open an issue</a>, we’d love to get your insights."}]},{"id":"required-html","type":"heading","en":"Required HTML","level":2},{"id":"required-html--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"There are two strict requirements for enabling RTL in Bootstrap-powered pages."},{"id":"required-html--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ol","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"required-html--item-1","type":"item","en":"Set <code>dir=&quot;rtl&quot;</code> on the <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> element."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"required-html--item-2","type":"item","en":"Add an appropriate <code>lang</code> attribute, like <code>lang=&quot;ar&quot;</code>, on the <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> element."}]}]},{"id":"required-html--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"From there, you’ll need to include an RTL version of our CSS. For example, here’s the stylesheet for our compiled and minified CSS with RTL enabled:"},{"id":"required-html--code-1","type":"code","value":"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.2.3/dist/css/bootstrap.rtl.min.css\" integrity=\"sha384-DOXMLfHhQkvFFp+rWTZwVlPVqdIhpDVYT9csOnHSgWQWPX0v5MCGtjCJbY6ERspU\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">","language":"html"},{"id":"starter-template","type":"heading","en":"Starter template","level":3},{"id":"starter-template--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"You can see the above requirements reflected in this modified RTL starter template."},{"id":"starter-template--code-1","type":"code","value":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">\n  <head>\n    <!-- Required meta tags -->\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n\n    <!-- Bootstrap CSS -->\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.2.3/dist/css/bootstrap.rtl.min.css\" integrity=\"sha384-DOXMLfHhQkvFFp+rWTZwVlPVqdIhpDVYT9csOnHSgWQWPX0v5MCGtjCJbY6ERspU\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">\n\n    <title>مرحبًا بالعالم!</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <h1>مرحبًا بالعالم!</h1>\n\n    <!-- Optional JavaScript; choose one of the two! -->\n\n    <!-- Option 1: Bootstrap Bundle with Popper -->\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.2.3/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js\" integrity=\"sha384-kenU1KFdBIe4zVF0s0G1M5b4hcpxyD9F7jL+jjXkk+Q2h455rYXK/7HAuoJl+0I4\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n\n    <!-- Option 2: Separate Popper and Bootstrap JS -->\n    <!--\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@popperjs/core@2.11.6/dist/umd/popper.min.js\" integrity=\"sha384-oBqDVmMz9ATKxIep9tiCxS/Z9fNfEXiDAYTujMAeBAsjFuCZSmKbSSUnQlmh/jp3\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.2.3/dist/js/bootstrap.min.js\" integrity=\"sha384-cuYeSxntonz0PPNlHhBs68uyIAVpIIOZZ5JqeqvYYIcEL727kskC66kF92t6Xl2V\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n    -->\n  </body>\n</html>","language":"html"},{"id":"rtl-examples","type":"heading","en":"RTL examples","level":3},{"id":"rtl-examples--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Get started with one of our several <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/examples/#rtl\">RTL examples</a>."},{"id":"approach","type":"heading","en":"Approach","level":2},{"id":"approach--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Our approach to building RTL support into Bootstrap comes with two important decisions that impact how we write and use our CSS:"},{"id":"approach--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ol","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"approach--item-1","type":"item","en":"<strong>First, we decided to build it with the <a href=\"https://rtlcss.com/\">RTLCSS</a> project.</strong> This gives us some powerful features for managing changes and overrides when moving from LTR to RTL. It also allows us to build two versions of Bootstrap from one codebase."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"approach--item-2","type":"item","en":"<strong>Second, we’ve renamed a handful of directional classes to adopt a logical properties approach.</strong> Most of you have already interacted with logical properties thanks to our flex utilities—they replace direction properties like <code>left</code> and <code>right</code> in favor <code>start</code> and <code>end</code>. That makes the class names and values appropriate for LTR and RTL without any overhead."}]}]},{"id":"approach--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"For example, instead of <code>.ml-3</code> for <code>margin-left</code>, use <code>.ms-3</code>."},{"id":"approach--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Working with RTL, through our source Sass or compiled CSS, shouldn’t be much different from our default LTR though."},{"id":"customize-from-source","type":"heading","en":"Customize from source","level":2},{"id":"customize-from-source--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"When it comes to <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/customize/sass/\">customization</a>, the preferred way is to take advantage of variables, maps, and mixins. This approach works the same for RTL, even if it’s post-processed from the compiled files, thanks to <a href=\"https://rtlcss.com/learn/getting-started/why-rtlcss/\">how RTLCSS works</a>."},{"id":"custom-rtl-values","type":"heading","en":"Custom RTL values","level":3},{"id":"custom-rtl-values--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Using <a href=\"https://rtlcss.com/learn/usage-guide/value-directives/\">RTLCSS value directives</a>, you can make a variable output a different value for RTL. For example, to decrease the weight for <code>$font-weight-bold</code> throughout the codebase, you may use the <code>/*rtl: {value}*/</code> syntax:"},{"id":"custom-rtl-values--code-1","type":"code","value":"$font-weight-bold: 700 #{/* rtl:600 */} !default;","language":"scss"},{"id":"custom-rtl-values--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Which would output to the following for our default CSS and RTL CSS:"},{"id":"custom-rtl-values--code-2","type":"code","value":"/* bootstrap.css */\ndt {\n  font-weight: 700 /* rtl:600 */;\n}\n\n/* bootstrap.rtl.css */\ndt {\n  font-weight: 600;\n}","language":"css"},{"id":"alternative-font-stack","type":"heading","en":"Alternative font stack","level":3},{"id":"alternative-font-stack--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"In the case you’re using a custom font, be aware that not all fonts support the non-Latin alphabet. To switch from Pan-European to Arabic family, you may need to use <code>/*rtl:insert: {value}*/</code> in your font stack to modify the names of font families."},{"id":"alternative-font-stack--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"For example, to switch from <code>Helvetica Neue</code> font for LTR to <code>Helvetica Neue Arabic</code> for RTL, your Sass code could look like this:"},{"id":"alternative-font-stack--code-1","type":"code","value":"$font-family-sans-serif:\n  Helvetica Neue #{\"/* rtl:insert:Arabic */\"},\n  // Cross-platform generic font family (default user interface font)\n  system-ui,\n  // Safari for macOS and iOS (San Francisco)\n  -apple-system,\n  // Chrome < 56 for macOS (San Francisco)\n  BlinkMacSystemFont,\n  // Windows\n  \"Segoe UI\",\n  // Android\n  Roboto,\n  // Basic web fallback\n  Arial,\n  // Linux\n  \"Noto Sans\",\n  // Sans serif fallback\n  sans-serif,\n  // Emoji fonts\n  \"Apple Color Emoji\", \"Segoe UI Emoji\", \"Segoe UI Symbol\", \"Noto Color Emoji\" !default;","language":"scss"},{"id":"ltr-and-rtl-at-the-same-time","type":"heading","en":"LTR and RTL at the same time","level":3},{"id":"ltr-and-rtl-at-the-same-time--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Need both LTR and RTL on the same page? Thanks to <a href=\"https://rtlcss.com/learn/usage-guide/string-map/\">RTLCSS String Maps</a>, this is pretty straightforward. Wrap your <code>@import</code>s with a class, and set a custom rename rule for RTLCSS:"},{"id":"ltr-and-rtl-at-the-same-time--code-1","type":"code","value":"/* rtl:begin:options: {\n  \"autoRename\": true,\n  \"stringMap\":[ {\n    \"name\": \"ltr-rtl\",\n    \"priority\": 100,\n    \"search\": [\"ltr\"],\n    \"replace\": [\"rtl\"],\n    \"options\": {\n      \"scope\": \"*\",\n      \"ignoreCase\": false\n    }\n  } ]\n} */\n.ltr {\n  @import \"../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/bootstrap\";\n}\n/*rtl:end:options*/","language":"scss"},{"id":"ltr-and-rtl-at-the-same-time--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"After running Sass then RTLCSS, each selector in your CSS files will be prepended by <code>.ltr</code>, and <code>.rtl</code> for RTL files. Now you’re able to use both files on the same page, and simply use <code>.ltr</code> or <code>.rtl</code> on your components wrappers to use one or the other direction."},{"id":"ltr-and-rtl-at-the-same-time--note-1","type":"note","tone":"warning","body":[{"id":"edge-cases-and-known-limitations","type":"heading","en":"Edge cases and known limitations","level":4},{"id":"edge-cases-and-known-limitations--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"While this approach is understandable, please pay attention to the following:"},{"id":"edge-cases-and-known-limitations--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ol","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"edge-cases-and-known-limitations--item-1","type":"item","en":"When switching <code>.ltr</code> and <code>.rtl</code>, make sure you add <code>dir</code> and <code>lang</code> attributes accordingly."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"edge-cases-and-known-limitations--item-2","type":"item","en":"Loading both files can be a real performance bottleneck: consider some <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/customize/optimize/\">optimization</a>, and maybe try to <a href=\"https://www.filamentgroup.com/lab/load-css-simpler/\">load one of those files asynchronously</a>."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"edge-cases-and-known-limitations--item-3","type":"item","en":"Nesting styles this way will prevent our <code>form-validation-state()</code> mixin from working as intended, thus require you tweak it a bit by yourself. <a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/issues/31223\">See #31223</a>."}]}]}]},{"id":"the-breadcrumb-case","type":"heading","en":"The breadcrumb case","level":2},{"id":"the-breadcrumb-case--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"The <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/components/breadcrumb//#changing-the-separator\">breadcrumb separator</a> is the only case requiring its own brand-new variable— namely <code>$breadcrumb-divider-flipped</code> —defaulting to <code>$breadcrumb-divider</code>."},{"id":"additional-resources","type":"heading","en":"Additional resources","level":2},{"id":"additional-resources--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"additional-resources--item-1","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://rtlcss.com/\">RTLCSS</a>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"additional-resources--item-2","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://rtlstyling.com/posts/rtl-styling\">RTL Styling 101</a>"}]}]}],"demos":[],"nav":[{"en":"Introduction","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Download","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/download/"},{"en":"Contents","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/contents/"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/browsers-devices/"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/javascript/"},{"en":"Webpack","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/webpack/"},{"en":"Parcel","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/parcel/"},{"en":"Vite","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/vite/"},{"en":"Accessibility","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/accessibility/"},{"en":"RFS","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/rfs/"},{"en":"RTL","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/rtl/"},{"en":"Contribute","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/contribute/"},{"en":"Overview","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/customize/overview/"},{"en":"Sass","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/customize/sass/"},{"en":"Options","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/customize/options/"},{"en":"Color","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/customize/color/"},{"en":"Components","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/customize/components/"},{"en":"CSS variables","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/customize/css-variables/"},{"en":"Optimize","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/customize/optimize/"},{"en":"Breakpoints","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/layout/breakpoints/"},{"en":"Containers","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/layout/containers/"},{"en"